# HTTP Methods

HTTP methods define the action to perform on a resource.

## 1. GET

Retrieves data from the server.

Example:

```
GET /students
```

Use Case:

- View all students
- Get user profile
- Retrieve product list

---

## 2. POST

Creates new data on the server.

Example:

```
POST /students
```

Use Case:

- Add a new student
- Register a new user

---

## 3. PUT

Updates an entire existing resource.

Example:

```
PUT /students/1
```

Use Case:

- Update all student details

---

## 4. PATCH

Updates only specific fields of a resource.

Example:

```
PATCH /students/1
```

Use Case:

- Update only the student's email or phone number

---

## 5. DELETE

Deletes an existing resource.

Example:

```
DELETE /students/1
```

Use Case:

- Remove a student record
- Delete a product

---

# HTTP Methods Summary

| Method | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| GET | Retrieve data |
| POST | Create new data |
| PUT | Update entire resource |
| PATCH | Update partial resource |
| DELETE | Delete data |

